  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "For each pair of real numbers \\(a \\neq b,\\) define the operation \\(\\star\\) as \\[ (a \\star b) = \\frac{a+b}{a-b}. \\]\n\nWhat is the value of \\(((1 \\star 2) \\star 3)?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)",
    "B": "\\(-\\dfrac{1}{5}\\)",
    "C": "\\(0\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)",
    "E": "This value is not defined."
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The parentheses tell us to evaluate \\(1\\star2\\) first. Substituting the ordered pair \\((1,2)\\) into the definition gives\n\\[\n1\\star2=\\frac{1+2}{1-2}=\\frac{3}{-1}=-3.\n\\]\nNow use \\(-3\\) as the first input and \\(3\\) as the second:\n\\[\n(-3)\\star3=\\frac{-3+3}{-3-3}=\\frac{0}{-6}=0.\n\\]\nThe denominators are \\(-1\\) and \\(-6\\), so both operations are defined. The value is \\(\\boxed{0}\\), choice C.",
